# How does light pick out a hero? Rembrandt's The Night Watch
tags: ["art history","light and shadow","rembrandt","composition","dutch golden age","visual hierarchy"]
thumb: "band \"Who's the hero?\" picture \"File:The_Night_Watch_-_HD.jpg\" colour"
teaches: ["art-history/rembrandt-technique","methods/compositional-lighting","concepts/visual-storytelling","history/dutch-portraiture"]
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | a warm, knowledgeable gallery guide, quietly amused","b":"gemini:Puck | a relaxed, good-humoured visitor with a dry, understated wit; curious, never exaggerated"}
prompt: "Who is lit, and who is left in shadow? Who is the glowing girl?"
next: {"title":"What can one candle do? La Tour's Magdalen with the Smoking Flame","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/how-painters-caught-light/04-what-can-one-candle-do-la-tour-s.cast"}

## The Night Watch: who gets the light
sources:
    - id: rijks
      title: The Night Watch (SK-C-5) and 10 things about Rembrandt's Night Watch
      authors: Rijksmuseum, Amsterdam
      year: 2026
      finding: 1642; captain Frans Banninck Cocq ordering lieutenant Willem van Ruytenburch to march the company; the hand's shadow on the lieutenant's coat with Amsterdam's arms between the fingers; the girl as the company's mascot; the name first recorded in 1797
      url: https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/en/stories/10-things/story/10-things-about-rembrandt-s-night-watch
    - id: wiki
      title: The Night Watch
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2026
      finding: Commissioned by the captain and seventeen militia members; darkened varnish gave the night-time name; the girl's chicken refers to the Kloveniers (arquebusiers)
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Night_Watch
    - id: gac
      title: The Night Watch
      authors: Rijksmuseum on Google Arts & Culture
      year: 2026
      finding: The more important people placed in the light, minor ones in the shade; the clawed chicken and pistol at the girl's belt are the company's symbols, she its mascot
      url: https://artsandculture.google.com/story/dALSivMco4xIJA

    card title "The Night Watch"

B: So this is The Night Watch. After Caravaggio's beam, more darkness, then?
    image art cites ["rijks","wiki"] credit "Rembrandt, 1642. Rijksmuseum, Amsterdam. Public domain." x 500 y 340 width 760 url https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/The_Night_Watch_-_HD.jpg/1920px-The_Night_Watch_-_HD.jpg look screen regions.back_men [0.25,0.33,0.4,0.2] regions.captain [0.41,0.45,0.14,0.52] regions.captain_face [0.44,0.47,0.075,0.12] regions.captain_hand [0.47,0.58,0.05,0.06] regions.cast [0.25,0.43,0.45,0.54] regions.chicken [0.29,0.665,0.045,0.075] regions.dark_top [0.2,0.04,0.55,0.3] regions.girl [0.265,0.58,0.1,0.28] regions.girl_face [0.3,0.585,0.045,0.055] regions.hand_shadow [0.595,0.668,0.032,0.055] regions.leaders [0.4,0.44,0.29,0.53] regions.lieutenant [0.55,0.49,0.135,0.47] regions.right_men [0.7,0.39,0.25,0.3] regions.whole [0.03,0.3,0.94,0.65]

    highlight art:dark_top strength soft duration 1.2

A: It isn't even night. This is Rembrandt, Amsterdam, 1642:
    portrait rembrandt x 300 y 505 width 150 of Rembrandt cameo true

    erase rembrandt

A: old brown varnish made it look dark, and the nickname stuck.
    highlight art:dark_top strength soft lift true

A: It's a portrait of citizen guards, nearly four metr (@highlight art:back_men art:right_men art:leaders lift true@)es high: the captain and seventeen of his men paid to be in it.

B: Then I'd expect a neat row, everyone equally bright.
    highlight art:whole strength soft rest dim lift true

A: That was the usual way. Rembrandt li (@highlight art:leaders lift true@)t only a few, so the light tells you who the hero is.

    ask "Who is in charge here? Tap him." spot captain on art voice a
        right: Yes: the man at the very front, in black.
        wrong: Look for the man at the front who is giving the orders, his hand held out.

    camera on ["art@[0.36,0.42,0.36,0.4]"]

A: The captain, Frans Banninck Cocq, in black with  (@highlight art:captain art:captain_face lift true@)a red sash: his face and collar catch the light.

B: I'd have picked the man in gold. He's the brightest thing in the room.
    highlight art:lieutenant lift true

A: That's his lieutenant, Willem van Ruytenburch, and his p (@highlight art:lieutenant art:captain lift true@)ale coat makes the captain's black stand out.

B: The captain's talking to him, with his hand out.
    point at.ref art:captain_hand gesture glow

    camera on ["art@[0.53,0.62,0.1,0.12]"]

A: Ordering the company to march. And the shad (@highlight art:hand_shadow lift true@)ow of that hand falls right on the lieutenant's coat.

A: Just where Amsterdam's coat of arms is embroidered: between the shadow's thumb and fingers.
    highlight art:hand_shadow strength strong lift true

B: The city, held in the captain's hand. Not subtle.
    highlight art:hand_shadow strength soft lift true

    camera reset true

A: Meanwhile, the men at the back paid their share too, and some got little more than a hat and a nose.
    highlight art:back_men art:right_men lift true

    ask "Tap the glowing figure who isn't a guardsman." spot girl on art voice a
        intro: But someone else is glowing, and it isn't a guard.
        right: There she is: a small girl, half hidden behind the musketeer in red.
        wrong: Look to the left of the captain, behind the man in red.

    camera on ["art@[0.2,0.52,0.24,0.38]"]

A: A small girl in gold, lit almost as brightly as the captain himself.
    highlight art:girl strength strong rest grey lift true

B: Whose daughter is she?
    highlight art:girl_face lift true

A: Probably nobody's. At her belt h (@highlight art:chicken lift true@)angs a dead chicken, its claws on show.

A: The company's emblem was a claw, so she carries their sign, like a mascot.
    highlight art:chicken art:girl lift true

B: A walking coat of arms. With poultry.
    highlight art:girl strength soft lift true

    camera on ["art@[0.2,0.38,0.55,0.6]"]

B: So the light isn't one beam this time. It's handed out: the leader, his lieutenant, and the company's sign.
    highlight art:captain art:lieutenant art:girl

A: Yes: Caravaggio's beam chose one man. Rembrandt's light builds a cast, a hero in front and a crowd behind.
    highlight art:cast strength soft rest grey lift true

    camera reset true

    quiz "A theatre director stages a crowd scene and wants the audience to see at once who leads it. Which lighting follows Rembrandt?" voice a
        right: The bright leader with a few lit helpers, and everyone else dim but still there: a hero, and a cast around him.
        wrong: Rembrandt didn't black the others out. Who stays visible, and how much?
        * Even light on the whole crowd
        * A spotlight on the leader, the rest black
        * Leader lit from below, crowd evenly lit
        + Bright leader, a few lit helpers, the rest dim but visible

B: Eighteen men paid for a portrait, and Rembrandt gave them a play instead.
    highlight art:whole strength soft lift true

